# Generated extraction output. Regenerable from data/raw/ + data/manifest.csv
# in seconds, and it duplicates every document's full text, so it is not worth
# committing. See data/README.md section 1.
data/processed/

# Operating System & IDE
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Library & Search sample corpus: the PDFs and the regenerable pipeline output.
# The manifest, the fetch log and sources.py ARE committed - they are the
# provenance record and the only unregenerable part.
data/sample_corpus/raw/
data/sample_corpus/processed/

# Compare version-pair corpus: the PDFs and the regenerable pipeline output.
# The manifest, the fetch log and sources.py ARE committed - they are the
# provenance record and the only unregenerable part. Same policy as the
# sample corpus above.
data/version_pairs/raw/
data/version_pairs/processed/

# Segment exports for teammates: the JSONL is regenerable from the database
# plus backend/scripts/export_segments.py, and bulk extracted document text
# does not belong in git (CLAUDE.md §16). The manifest and README ARE
# committed - they are the provenance record, like data/manifest.csv.
exports/*.jsonl

# Recoverable backups taken before the 2026-11-16 integration cleanup.
# pg_dump archives and copies of removed files: large, binary, and not source.
# Recovery instructions are in
# backend/docs/FINAL_FRONTEND_BACKEND_INTEGRATION_REPORT.md section 11.
backups/

# What the running application ingests, kept out of the original corpus's
# data/raw and data/processed on purpose (see that report, section 9.3).
# Regenerable by re-uploading the source PDFs.
data/app/
